From a6fbe6125b6b1da47e62073372c462dc3cad5da6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexey Lapin <a.lapin03@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:27:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): show and edit the Hone feedback on Pi replies

The feedback under the newest Pi reply expands to every entry in full.
Either thumb opens a popover that lists the entries Hone holds for the
session, each editable in place or removable, above the field for a new
entry. The pressed thumb follows the newest rated entry.

The new hone.replaceFeedback RPC sends the whole edited list to Hone's
PUT /api/traces/{id}/feedback. hone.threadFeedback now returns parsed
entries, and a multi-line comment is folded into one line so each entry
stays one line in Hone.
